## Source audit and change

- Java Push send-back uses virtual `MessageExt.getStoreHost()` to select a
  broker address when no broker name is available. Rust previously read only
  the stored base host.
- Added `MessageExtSubtype` hooks for `getStoreHost` and `setStoreHost` and
  routed `MessageExt::store_host` and `set_store_host` through them.
- The invoked Java direct-consume fixture sets a host through the custom
  setter, records the custom getter as present, and compares its setter count.
  A Rust Push send-back regression sets the base host to `127.0.0.1:10911` and
  the custom getter to `127.0.0.1:10912`; the request uses the custom endpoint.
- Updated the Phase 6, Phase 10 and Phase 18 records and release checklist.

